      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A study of 20 patients with essential hypertension, stage IIB, asymmetrical myocardial hypertrophy and chest pains has suggested that the pain syndrome, presenting as \"possible angina\", positive functional tests and reduced label accumulation around the ventricular septum may be indicative of coronary insufficiency."},
